---
import BaseHead from '../../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../../../components/Header.astro';

const pageTitle = 'ERT Game Web';
const pageDescription = 'A multiplayer game application showcasing full-stack development with Express.js backend and Vue.js frontend.';
const repoUrl = 'https://github.com/lefos13/ert-game-web';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription} />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Header />
    <main class="page">
      <section class="hero">
        <p class="eyebrow">Project Spotlight</p>
        <h1>{pageTitle}</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          A real-time multiplayer game platform where players submit answers, vote on responses, and 
          compete for points. Built with Express.js, Vue 3, TypeScript, and featuring comprehensive 
          admin controls and session management.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="content">
        <h2>What I Built</h2>
        <p>
          ERT Game is a complete full-stack application that demonstrates modern web development practices. 
          The platform supports multiple players simultaneously, real-time game state management, and provides 
          both player and administrator interfaces with distinct workflows.
        </p>

        <h3>Key Features</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Real-time multiplayer gameplay with round-based question-answer mechanics.</li>
          <li>Dual-interface design: streamlined player view and comprehensive admin dashboard.</li>
          <li>Session management with voting system, point tracking, and game history exports.</li>
          <li>Automated installation scripts for Windows (PowerShell) and Linux/macOS (Bash).</li>
          <li>RESTful API with health checks, CORS configuration, and proper error handling.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Technical Architecture</h3>
        <p>
          The backend runs on Express.js with JSON file-based persistence for session data and round status. 
          The Vue 3 frontend leverages TypeScript, Pinia state management, and modern Sass modules for styling. 
          Component organization follows domain-driven principles, separating player, admin, and shared UI elements.
        </p>

        <h3>Stack at a Glance</h3>
        <div class="stack-grid">
          <div>
            <h4>Backend</h4>
            <p>Node.js, Express, RESTful APIs, JSON persistence</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h4>Frontend</h4>
            <p>Vue 3, TypeScript, Vite, Pinia, Sass modules</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h4>DevOps</h4>
            <p>Automated installers, environment detection, health checks</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h3>API Highlights</h3>
        <p>
          The server exposes comprehensive endpoints for session management, round status tracking, and player 
          operations including joining, answering, voting, and point updates. All routes return consistent JSON 
          responses with proper HTTP status codes.
        </p>

        <h3>Outcome</h3>
        <p>
          The application has been deployed and tested across different environments. The installer scripts 
          detect IP addresses automatically and configure both server and client for immediate use. The 
          architecture scales comfortably for local network gameplay and supports export functionality for 
          game analytics.
        </p>

        <p class="cta">
          Explore the repository, check out the component architecture, or run the game locally:
          <a href={repoUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{repoUrl}</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  .page {
    margin: 0 auto;
    max-width: 960px;
    padding: 3rem 1.5rem 4rem;
  }

  .hero {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    color: var(--accent, #4b63ff);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    max-width: 48ch;
  }

  .content h2,
  .content h3 {
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .content ul {
    margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem;
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
  }

  .stack-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 720px) {
    .stack-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  .stack-grid > div {
    background: white;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
    box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);
  }

  .stack-grid h4 {
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
    color: var(--accent, #4b63ff);
  }

  .cta {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent, #4b63ff);
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    padding-left: 1rem;
  }
</style>
